        "original_id": "309d76fa-afab-53b4-9a2f-caa22a7c9636",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: St Vincents Hall, Grantham\n- People: Richard Hornsby, Herbert Akroyd Stuart\n- Companies: Richard Hornsby & Sons\n- Products: Hornsby-Akroyd oil engine\n- Topics: Gothic Revival architecture, engine and machinery manufacturing\n\nFacts:\n- In 1868, St Vincents Hall in Grantham was built as a Gothic Revival mansion for industrialist Richard Hornsby.\n- Richard Hornsby founded Richard Hornsby & Sons as an engine and machinery manufacturing company.\n- Richard Hornsby & Sons was a pioneer in manufacturing the oil engine developed by Herbert Akroyd Stuart.\n- Richard Hornsby & Sons marketed Herbert Akroyd Stuart's oil engine under the \"Hornsby-Akroyd\" name.",
